101f4014afce5a997a8c7bb4b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeff Gilbert \u003cjgilbert@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1676636 - [angle] Cherry-pick compressed tex depth stride fix. r=lsalzman, a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D102523", "files": ["gfx/angle/checkout/src/libANGLE/formatutils.cpp", "gfx/angle/cherry_picks.txt"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ba9becdcf15c3b067520fbfe6a9a3d2d6421efcb", "parents": ["073a47a8d73d43494317681944eb475018081b70"], "tags": []}], "date": 1612465419, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "jcristau@mozilla.com"}, "189": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 15a5f89243daa17a6fa319424bdf3d888622a861 with FIREFOX_78_7_1esr_BUILD1 a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "140d2e0ad7c73d2561ba765610ec637e05c63049", "parents": ["ba9becdcf15c3b067520fbfe6a9a3d2d6421efcb"], "tags": []}], "date": 1612473894, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "190": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1686825 - Don't perform PropertyKey::fromPinnedString if the string creation failed, r=pbone a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D102483", "files": ["js/xpconnect/src/XPCWrappedNativeInfo.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "47137fbd429408c0a4ddd98a0eff000513e2212c", "parents": ["140d2e0ad7c73d2561ba765610ec637e05c63049"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cameron Kaiser \u003cspectre@floodgap.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1690152 - on ppc64 properly skip parameter slots if we overflow GPRs while still having FPRs to burn. r=tcampbell, a=pascalc\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D103724", "files": ["xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcinvoke_ppc64_linux.cpp", "xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcstubs_ppc64_linux.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2ffdb46e8a4913f601c627e90ec2380f5f0ece04", "parents": ["47137fbd429408c0a4ddd98a0eff000513e2212c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Haik Aftandilian \u003chaftandilian@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1660583 - [Rosetta] Flash plugin process crashes on ESR 78 startup under Rosetta. r=spohl, a=RyanVM\n\nAllow access to the `hw.memsize` sysctl in the Flash sandbox to prevent Flash plugin crashes under Rosetta.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D103371", "files": ["security/sandbox/mac/SandboxPolicyFlash.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "df9373ab9b71eef71742e1134239e2d853fc5c7e", "parents": ["2ffdb46e8a4913f601c627e90ec2380f5f0ece04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1689395 - Backport some upstream OTS commits. r=jfkthame, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D103339", "files": ["gfx/ots/src/glyf.cc", "gfx/ots/src/glyf.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cc7a75e521ee1087b0383c1afb055ecefd39797c", "parents": ["df9373ab9b71eef71742e1134239e2d853fc5c7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "William Durand \u003cwill+git@drnd.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1686187 - Use AMO API v4. r=robwu, a=RyanVM\n\nAMO API v3 is deprecated and we should now use API v4. Both versions are pretty similar even if the [changelog](https://addons-server.readthedocs.io/en/latest/topics/api/overview.html#v4-api-changelog) appears to be large (we mainly added new features).\n\nI reviewed our usage of the AMO API in FF and diff'ed the API responses. I didn't notice any main difference except for `about:addons` disco, which is why I removed some code related to old properties.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D101945", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/newtab/lib/CFRPageActions.jsm", "mobile/android/app/mobile.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/aboutaddons.html", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/aboutaddons.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_html_discover_view.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/discovery/api_response.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cf0507a516ff432af05eff5337b7ffdccebdc128", "parents": ["cc7a75e521ee1087b0383c1afb055ecefd39797c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonfreed@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1684116 [wpt PR 27007] - Fix serialization for \u003cnoscript\u003e contents when script is disabled, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix serialization for \u003cnoscript\u003e contents when script is disabled\n\nPrevious to this CL, serialization for \u003cnoscript\u003e nodes in a\ndocument with (per spec) no execution context would still *not*\nescape (e.g. '\u003c' --\u003e '&lt;') the contents. This allowed a sanitizer\nbypass.\n\nI added a fairly comprehensive test of the many fragment parser entry\npoints here. Before this CL (and on other browsers):\n - Chrome would never escape \u003cnoscript\u003e contents. (This bug)\n - Firefox would never escape \u003cnoscript\u003e contents. (Should raise a bug)\n - Safari *always* escapes \u003cnoscript\u003e contents, *even* when it\n   shouldn't, such as with div.innerHTML, div.insertAdjacentHTML,\n   and document.write on the main document. (Should raise a bug)\n\nAn additional set of differences showed up for the *parsing* escaping\nbehavior:\n - Chrome would (and still does) de-escape \u003cnoscript\u003e contents when\n   parsing in a script-disabled context, such as DOMParser or\n   createHTMLDocument.innerHTML. It does *not* de-escape \u003cnoscript\u003e\n   contents in script-enabled contexts, such as div.innerHTML and\n   document.write. This all seems correct to me.\n - Safari behaves identically to Chrome here (correct).\n - Firefox de-escapes \u003cnoscript\u003e contents in some cases (e.g.\n   XMLHTTPRequest, document.write) but not others (e.g.\n   template.innerHTML, createHTMLDocument.innerHTML, and\n   createHTMLDocument.createContextualFragment).\n\nI looked for a spec issue, but didn't find one. If there really isn't\na spec issue for this, we should raise one.\n\nFixed: 1160635\nChange-Id: I361a72409093e69b074495c475e9d647c6c58300\nCq-Do-Not-Cancel-Tryjobs: true\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/2602447\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mason Freed \u003cmasonfreed@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/master@{#839214}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 65e68547032c551e8765245621a9aac70e5d5a3d\nwpt-pr: 27007", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/serializing-html-fragments/escaping.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "fc1c60983fbc4cb3a29d755b590f6b6e7edd8b8b", "parents": ["cf0507a516ff432af05eff5337b7ffdccebdc128"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1684116 [wpt PR 27007] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 27007\nwpt-type: metadata", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/syntax/serializing-html-fragments/escaping.html.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f0716e84d80f341b0286e67e39d2c1480023af3c", "parents": ["fc1c60983fbc4cb3a29d755b590f6b6e7edd8b8b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1683627 - Make \u003cnoscript\u003e escaping conditional on whether scripting is enabled. r=smaug, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D102159", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/syntax/serializing-html-fragments/escaping.html.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9cc6abd00b88b8f8f1756222cec3e0eded0ba89c", "parents": ["f0716e84d80f341b0286e67e39d2c1480023af3c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 786797 - Check for integer overflow when computing new buffer sizes. r=smaug, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D102592", "files": ["parser/html/javasrc/MetaScanner.java", "parser/html/javasrc/Portability.java", "parser/html/javasrc/Tokenizer.java", "parser/html/nsHtml5MetaScanner.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5Portability.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5Portability.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5Tokenizer.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4d73b6090b1154f17536c26acc461ff519152e43", "parents": ["9cc6abd00b88b8f8f1756222cec3e0eded0ba89c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1612476819, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "191": {"changesets": [{"author": "Rob Wu \u003crob@robwu.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1678734 - Fix crash in StreamFilter with view-source. r=mixedpuppy, a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D100146", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_webRequest_viewsource_StreamFilter.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell-e10s.ini", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell-remote.ini", "toolkit/components/extensions/webrequest/StreamFilterParent.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "432f7db58ff0e99c5e559c4341ac01659760a0d4", "parents": ["4d73b6090b1154f17536c26acc461ff519152e43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1676785 - Simplify XUL special code-path for \u003cinput\u003e value setter. r=masayuki, a=RyanVM\n\nThis allows us to remove nsISelectionControlle